{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "Soulcasting turns one material into another. A Soulcaster is the fabrial that does it, or the person who uses one.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "5" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Soulcasting turns one material into another, using the Surge of Transformation. Most of it is done with fabrials called Soulcasters; Surgebinders can do it without one.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "70" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Soulcasting turns one material into another, such as stone into smoke or rock into grain. A Soulcaster can mean the fabrial that does it or the person who uses one.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "5" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Soulcasting uses Stormlight so fast that it can crack the gemstones holding it.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "5" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Khriss's Ars Arcanum names Transformation as the Surge of Soulcasting: it changes an object into one of the Ten Essences.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }]
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Uses",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "7" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "2" },
            {
